enal sodium and potassium excretion during fetal life and newborn period</article-title><source>Dev Pharmacol Ther</source><year>1980</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>201</fpage><lpage>216</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7002509</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B55"><label>55</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gimonet</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Bussieres</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Medjebeur</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Gasser</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Lelongt</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Laborde</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nephrogenesis and angiotensin II receptor subtypes gene expression in the fetal lamb</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><year>1998</year><volume>274</volume><fpage>F1062</fpage><lpage>F1069</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9841497</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><p>Expression of glucocorticoid receptor (GR) and mineralocorticoid receptor (MR) and their target genes in lungs of 80-, 100-, 120-, 130- and 145-day fetuses and day 1 and day 7 neonatal lambs. Data are depicted as mRNA fold changes relative to 80 days. (<bold>a</bold>) GR, (<bold>b</bold>) MR, (<bold>c</bold>) 11&#x003b2;-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase 1 (11&#x003b2;-HSD1), (<bold>d</bold>) 11&#x003b2;-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase 2 (11&#x003b2;-HSD2), (<bold>e</bold>) serum and glucocorticoid-induced kinase (Sgk-1), (<bold>f</bold>) epithelial sodium channel (ENaC&#x003b1;), and (<bold>g</bold>) sodium, potassium ATPase (Na,K-ATPase &#x003b1;1). Superscripts a&#x02013;g indicate &#x00394;C<sub>t</sub> values significantly different by ANOVA: a = vs. 80 days; b = vs. 100 days; c = vs. 120 days; d = vs. 130 days; e = vs. 145 days; f = vs. 1 day neonate; g = vs. 7 days neonate.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="neo-0095-0047-g01"/></fig><fig id="F2" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 2</label><caption><p>Expression of MR and GR and their target genes expression in renal cortex of 80-, 100-, 120-, 130- and 145-day fetuses and day 1 and day 7 neonatal lambs. Data depicted as mRNA fold changes relative to 80 days. Panelsand symbols are as described in figure 1.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="neo-0095-0047-g02"/></fig><fig id="F3" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 3</label><caption><p>Expression of MR and GR and their target genes in renal medulla of 80-, 100-, 120-, 130- and 145-day fetuses and day 1 and day 7 neonatal lambs. Data depicted as mRNA fold changes relative to 80 days. Panels and symbols are as described in figure 1.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="neo-0095-0047-g03"/></fig><fig id="F4" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 4</label><caption><p>Expression of MR and GR and their target genes in small intestine of 80-, 100-, 120-, 130- and 145-day fetuses and day 1 and day 7 neonatal lambs. Data depicted as mRNA fold changes relative to 80 days. Panels and symbols are as described in figure 1.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="neo-0095-0047-g04"/></fig><fig id="F5" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 5</label><caption><p>Abundance of ENaC&#x003b1; protein (<bold>a</bold>, <bold>b</bold>) and Na,K-ATPase (<bold>c</bold>, <bold>d</bold>) and Sgk-1 (<bold>e</bold>) in homogenates of lung (<bold>a</bold>, <bold>c</bold>, <bold>e</bold>), and in membrane fractions prepared from lung (<bold>b</bold>, <bold>d</bold>) of 80-, 120-, 130- and 145-day fetuses and day 1 neonatal lambs. Data are corrected for abundance of &#x003b2;-actin in the same immunoblot and are expressed in arbitrary units. Superscripts a&#x02013;e indicate values significantly different by ANOVA: a = vs. 80 days; b = vs. 120 days; c = vs. 130 days; d = vs. 145 days; e = vs. 1 day lamb.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="neo-0095-0047-g05"/></fig><fig id="F6" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 6</label><caption><p>Abundance of ENaC&#x003b1; protein (<bold>a</bold>, <bold>b</bold>), Na,K-ATPase (<bold>c</bold>, <bold>d</bold>) and Sgk-1 (<bold>e</bold>) in homogenates of renal cortex (<bold>a</bold>, <bold>c</bold>), and in membrane fractions prepared from renal cortex (<bold>b</bold>, <bold>d</bold>) of 80-, 120-, 130- and 145-day fetuses and day 1 neonatal lambs. Data are expressed in arbitrary units. Superscripts a&#x02013;d indicate values significantly different by ANOVA: a = vs. 80 days; b = vs. 120 days; c = vs. 130 days; d = vs. 145 days.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="neo-0095-0047-g06"/></fig><fig id="F7" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 7</label><caption><p>Abundance of ENaC&#x003b1; protein (<bold>a</bold>, <bold>b</bold>), Na,K-ATPase (<bold>c</bold>, <bold>d</bold>), and Sgk-1 (<bold>e</bold>) in homogenates of renal medulla (<bold>a</bold>, <bold>c</bold>), and in membrane fractions prepared from renal medulla (<bold>b</bold>, <bold>d</bold>) of 100-, 120-, 130- and 145-day fetuses and day 1 neonatal lambs. Data are expressed in arbitrary units. Superscripts a&#x02013;d indicate &#x00394;C<sub>t</sub> values significantly different by ANOVA: a = vs. 100 days; b = vs. 120 days; d = vs. 145 days.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="neo-0095-0047-g07"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Average relative expression of genes in renal cortex, medulla and small intestine as compared to lung at the same developmental age (values are calculated from the mean ACT compared to 18S for the animals in each group)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="rows"><thead><tr valign="top"><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Lung</th><th align="l